<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spetses</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spetses is a small Greek island off the eastern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, near the entrance to the Argolic Gulf. Like Hydra it built a merchant fleet in the 18th century, and its ships fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence">Greek War of Independence</a>, when the island's Laskarina Bouboulina commanded vessels against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spetses.jpg" alt="Spetses" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Housen · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:20090730_spetsai033.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
